{%- comment -%}
  The metal circle for a material value (2026-10-28, owner: products with stones drop the separate colour option, and
  „the circle colors stay the same … just to be on jewelry material“). Shopify allows three options; a ring with size,
  material and stone has no room for the colour option whose swatches drew the circles, so a material value with no
  swatch of its own gets the same picture the colour option's swatches use (Shopify Files, by name).

  Prints a CSS background value — url(…) or rgb(…) — or nothing when the value names no metal.

  Accepts:
  - name: {String} the option value's name, e.g. „14К жълто злато“
  - width: {Number} the file's width in px (optional, 160 by default)

  Usage:
  {%- capture dot -%}{% render 'cj-metal-swatch', name: value.name %}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign cj_metal_down = name | append: '' | downcase
  assign cj_metal_file = ''
  assign cj_metal_rgb = ''
  if cj_metal_down contains 'бяло злато' or cj_metal_down contains 'white gold'
    assign cj_metal_file = 'ChatGPT_Image_Sep_27_2026_06_12_59_PM.png'
  elsif cj_metal_down contains 'розово злато' or cj_metal_down contains 'rose gold'
    assign cj_metal_file = 'ChatGPT_Image_Sep_26_2026_05_00_24_PM.png'
  elsif cj_metal_down contains 'жълто злато' or cj_metal_down contains 'yellow gold'
    assign cj_metal_file = 'ChatGPT_Image_Sep_26_2026_04_59_35_PM.png'
  elsif cj_metal_down contains 'сребро' or cj_metal_down contains 'silver'
    assign cj_metal_rgb = 'rgb(201 203 207)'
  endif
  assign cj_metal_width = width | default: 160
  if cj_metal_file != ''
    assign cj_metal_image = images[cj_metal_file]
    if cj_metal_image != blank
      echo cj_metal_image | image_url: width: cj_metal_width, height: cj_metal_width, crop: 'center' | prepend: 'url(' | append: ')'
    endif
  elsif cj_metal_rgb != ''
    echo cj_metal_rgb
  endif
-%}
